check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3149021Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3156691Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3247097Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3255461Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3256030Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3256771Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3257016Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3257252Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3257808Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3258186Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3258395Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3259631Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3259942Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3260696Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3261346Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3262124Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3262609Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3262788Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3263054Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3263417Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3263662Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3264105Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3264277Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3264522Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3264710Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3265185Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3265785Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3266154Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3266474Z I will:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3266712Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3266969Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3267463Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3268081Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3268551Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3268963Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3269526Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3270053Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3270548Z    /root
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3280504Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3281257Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3289986Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3290580Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3290961Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3291916Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3292497Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3308545Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3309090Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3317762Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3318371Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3319075Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3319486Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3319682Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3319964Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3320282Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3320785Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3321029Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3321163Z If you would like to
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3321552Z see the output, try like this:
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3321754Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3321996Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3322475Z   $ sh ./install-nix
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3322715Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3322728Z 
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3323037Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3327961Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
check (ubuntu-24.04-arm)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:29.3328619Z been installed on this system.
