check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5644588Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5654234Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5748757Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5758161Z ^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5758938Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5759605Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5759834Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5760030Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5760675Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5760956Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5761603Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5762226Z    if you are ready to continue.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5762759Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5763245Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5763869Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5764727Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5765198Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5765431Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5765717Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5766054Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5766428Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5766941Z    can use Nix.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5767113Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5767273Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5767485Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5767865Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5768472Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5771836Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5772065Z I will:
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5773815Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5774173Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5774733Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5775286Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5775822Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5776198Z  - install Nix in /nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5776565Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5777094Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5777580Z    /root
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5786612Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5787153Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5797352Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5797859Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5798188Z 
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5799508Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
check (ubuntu-latest)	UNKNOWN STEP	2026-11-06T02:54:20.5799965Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
